## Today: Let's create some data visualizations + start some data analysis

## Learning Goals

By the end of this session, learners will be able to

1.  Build and customize basic data visualizations in ggplot2 (including histograms, bar graphs, scatterplots, box plots, and violin plots).
2.  Create custom themes and reusable function wrappers to apply consistent formatting across plots.
3.  Visualize linear regression results using coefficient forest plots.

In this lesson, we will explore the grammar of graphics using `ggplot2` to visualize data from raw counts to statistical models. We will cover how to build plots layer-by-layer, customize visual properties, create reusable styling functions, and visualize multiple linear regression outputs using forest plots.

